            "review_title": "Review at Yo Yummy Oi Thao Dien",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n1\nSingapore-Malaysian food haven, food court style\nApr 2021 • Couples\nA collection of Singapore-Malaysian good food: Chinese+Hongkong, Malay, Indian, Vietnamese food stores all under one roof, just like the many beloved food courts in these two countries. Beer and drinks available too. Indoor seating with air-condition, Outdoor seating under a huge cooling tentage.\n\nYou can find favourites likes: Satays, roti paratha/ roti canai, seafood dishes, oyster omelette, Hong Kong style roasted meats, and the NUMEROUS noodle/rice dishes such as prawn-broth noodles, mee rebus, mee siam, hor fun, etc can all be found here. Pretty awesome. Our big plate of chilli crab dish with free mantous (fried bread) for dipping was just 500,000vnd. Noodle dishes were below 100,000vnd. A nice touch selling some instant noodles, kopi (coffee), teh (teas) and even canned abalones from that region too.\n\nThose who miss these foods: you'll be glad to find authentic ones here all under one roof.\nThose who ain't from around Malaysia/Singapore, you'll find it exciting to try different cuisines at one place!\nRead more\nWritten May 7, 2021",
